'' __FB_MT__ ACROSS UNITS, the threaded one first (review ARCH-05, LATER-PLAN G step 4: the
'' sticky state a multi-unit build shows). fbc-modern 1.20, 'fbc thread.bas plain.bas': the
'' thread unit sees -1 after its own call, and so does every unit compiled after it. The
'' second unit's top-level code runs first, as a module constructor (ctor-order-run.test).
'' tiko gave the thread unit 0: it turned -mt on after LOWERING the unit, not as the call
'' was parsed.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/mt-order/thread.bas tests/codegen/src/mt-order/plain.bas -o tests/codegen/mtorder1.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/mtorder1.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: plain unit: -1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: thread unit: -1
